For a conditionally convergent series the order of summation matters:
$
  sum_(n=1)^oo (-1)^(n+1) (1)/(n) = 1 - (1)/(2) + (1)/(3) - (1)/(4) + ...
$
Rearranged as
$
  (1-(1)/(2)) - (1)/(4) + ((1)/(3)-(1)/(6)) - (1)/(8) + ((1)/(5)-(1)/(10)) - ... = (1)/(2) sum_(n=1)^oo (-1)^(n+1) (1)/(n),
$
the series sums to half its original value: two positive terms are traded for one negative term each round, so convergence is preserved but the sum changes.
